## 📁 File-by-File Breakdown

### Backend — `route_optimizer/`

---

#### [app.py](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/app.py)

**Role:** Flask web server — the REST API layer and orchestrator.

| Endpoint | Method | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `/` | GET | Serves the static home page and resets state |
| `/optimize` | POST | Accepts `source`, `destination`, `preferences`; kicks off optimization in a **background thread** |
| `/status` | GET | Returns current `route_data` (polled by frontend every 500ms) |
| `/marker-close` | POST | Signal from frontend that the animated marker reached a waypoint — unblocks the backend thread |
| `/reset` | GET | Resets all server state (stops threads, clears route data) |

**Key Design Patterns:**
- **[RouteState](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/app.py#12-42) class** — Thread-safe state management using `threading.Lock`. Holds the [RouteGraph](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/graph.py#15-288) instance, the active optimization thread, and the shared `route_data` dict.
- **Background threading** — Route optimization runs in a separate thread ([run_optimization](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/app.py#108-126)), so the HTTP server stays responsive during computation.
- **Event-based synchronization** — `marker_close_event` (a `threading.Event`) bridges the frontend animation with backend computation. The backend **waits** until the frontend confirms the marker reached the next node before computing the next segment.

---

#### [graph.py](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/graph.py) — ⭐ Core Algorithm

**Role:** The brain of the system — route generation, graph construction, A\* optimization, and dynamic rerouting.

**Class: [RouteGraph](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/graph.py#15-288)** — initializes all 4 API clients + the Heuristic engine.

| Method | Purpose |
|---|---|
| [haversine_distance(coord1, coord2)](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/graph.py#27-58) | Calculates great-circle distance between two lat/lng points (used to filter nodes too close together, threshold: 250m) |
| [generate_all_routes(source, dest)](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/graph.py#162-191) | Calls Google Maps Directions API with `alternatives=True` to get all possible routes. Extracts each step's end location as a graph node. Filters nodes closer than 250m to avoid clutter |
| [calculate_heuristic_values(route, prefs)](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/graph.py#192-221) | For each segment (edge) of a route: fetches traffic, weather, elevation, and AQI data **in parallel** (ThreadPoolExecutor, 10 workers). Computes penalties and the weighted heuristic score |
| [construct_graph(route, heuristics)](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/graph.py#242-248) | Builds a directed weighted graph (adjacency dict) from route nodes + heuristic scores as edge weights |
| [merge_graphs(graphs)](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/graph.py#249-259) | Merges multiple route graphs into one, keeping the **minimum weight** for duplicate edges — this creates the "super-graph" for A\* |
| [apply_a_star(graph, start, goal)](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/graph.py#260-284) | Classic A\* pathfinding on the merged graph. Uses [heuristic_estimate()](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/heuristic.py#36-43) as the h-function. Returns the optimal path |
| [find_optimal_route(source, dest, prefs)](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/graph.py#59-83) | End-to-end pipeline: generate routes → calculate heuristics → build graphs → merge → A\* → return optimal coords |
| [dynamic_route_optimization(...)](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/graph.py#84-161) | **The main loop**: walks the optimal route node-by-node. At each node, re-fetches alternative routes, recalculates if better paths exist, and **dynamically reroutes**. Synchronizes with the frontend via `marker_close_event` |

**Data Flow within [dynamic_route_optimization](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/graph.py#84-161):**
```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Start: source → destination"] --> B["find_optimal_route()"]
    B --> C["Walk route node by node"]
    C --> D["Append next node to final_route"]
    D --> E["Wait for frontend marker to reach node"]
    E --> F["generate_all_routes from current node to destination"]
    F --> G{">1 alternative?"}
    G -->|Yes| H["Recalculate: heuristics → graph → A* → new optimal route"]
    G -->|No| I["Continue on current route"]
    H --> J["Update current_route with new optimal path"]
    I --> K{"Reached destination?"}
    J --> K
    K -->|No| C
    K -->|Yes| L["Mark status = completed"]
```

---

#### [heuristic.py](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/heuristic.py)

**Role:** Computes the multi-factor heuristic score for each route segment.

**Scoring Formula:**
```
Score = Wt × T  +  We × E  +  Wa × A  +  Σ(Wi × Pi)
```

| Symbol | Meaning | Calculation |
|---|---|---|
| `T` | Travel time | `distance / speed` |
| `E` | Emissions | `distance × emission_factor / fuel_efficiency` |
| `A` | Air quality index (normalized) | `AQI / 500` |
| `Pi` | Penalties (traffic, weather, terrain, wind) | From [Penalties](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/models/penalties.py#4-36) class |
| `Wt, We, Wa` | Dynamic weights | Derived from user preferences (sliders) |
| `Wi` | Penalty weights | Fixed at 0.025 each |

- **[heuristic_estimate(distance_remaining)](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/heuristic.py#36-43)** — Admissible A\* heuristic: assumes best-case speed (100 km/h), minimal emissions, and zero AQI.
- Supports multiple **vehicle types**: petrol, diesel, hybrid, electric, truck, bus — each with different CO₂ emission factors.

---

#### [models/penalties.py](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/route_optimizer/models/penalties.py)

**Role:** Calculates four penalty values that penalize unfavorable conditions.

| Penalty | Formula / Logic |
|---|---|
| `Pt` (Traffic) | [(actual_duration - free_flow_duration) / free_flow_duration](file:///f:/college%20files/projects/Raven-AI-Route-Optimizer-main/frontend/src/App.js#7-480) — congestion ratio |
| `Pw` (Weather) | Lookup map: Clear=0, Light rain=0.2, Heavy rain=0.5, Snow=0.7, Fog=0.5 |
| `Pter` (Terrain) | `elevation_change / distance` — steepness ratio |
| `Pwind` (Wind) | `wind_speed / 20` — normalized to max 20 m/s |

