## 🔗 Integration & Data Flow Summary

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    subgraph User
        FORM["Source + Dest + Preferences"]
    end

    subgraph Frontend
        REACT["React App"]
        MAP["Leaflet Map"]
    end

    subgraph Backend
        FLASK["Flask Server"]
        THREAD["Background Thread"]
        RGRAPH["RouteGraph"]
    end

    subgraph External
        GM["Google Maps"]
        AQ["Air Quality API"]
        EL["Elevation API"]
        WA["WeatherAPI"]
    end

    FORM -->|POST /optimize| FLASK
    FLASK -->|spawns| THREAD
    THREAD --> RGRAPH
    RGRAPH --> GM
    RGRAPH --> AQ
    RGRAPH --> EL
    RGRAPH --> WA
    RGRAPH -->|updates route_data dict| FLASK
    FLASK -->|GET /status response| REACT
    REACT --> MAP
    MAP -->|POST /marker-close| FLASK
    FLASK -->|Event.set()| THREAD
```

**The critical synchronization mechanism:**
1. Backend computes next waypoint → updates `route_data["final_route"]` → **blocks** on `marker_close_event.wait()`
2. Frontend polls `/status` → detects new node → animates marker → when marker reaches node → sends `POST /marker-close`
3. Backend receives signal → `marker_close_event.set()` → unblocks thread → computes next segment
4. This creates a **synchronized lock-step** between backend computation and frontend visualization

